{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":722152,"ns":0,"title":"Alphabet of human thought","extract":"The alphabet of human thought (Latin: alphabetum cogitationum humanarum) is a concept originally proposed by Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz that provides a universal way to represent and analyze ideas and relationships by breaking down their component pieces. All ideas are compounded from a very small number of simple ideas which can be represented by a unique character.","description":"Hypothetical language created by Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}